  "_doc": "A star system (openspec/changes/patrol-mission design 2; flight-and-navigation 13's system file): the system frame has its origin at the star's centre, x and z in the plane of the planets, +y north; positions are metres. The bodies stand where they are at the mission's epoch (rails, flight-and-navigation 8, come later). A station's attitude turns its own frame (its axis +x) into the system's; a berth is a pose in the station's frame (where the docked Tern's origin sits, and its attitude there) and a departure path in the berth's own frame (the docked Tern's), each leg ending at a point with the most it may be flown at, so a berth works whatever shape its station has. A point of interest's arrival point is an offset from it, where a jump to it ends. A body's look is the sky program's planet (data/space/exterior.json's fields). Read by sc-core::system.",
